# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WALL OVERRIDES
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The auto-detected walls are pulled from the photo -- they're only as good
# as what's actually built on the board. If you know a specific edge is
# wrong (e.g. you've confirmed by eye that a "wall" the detector found is
# actually open, or you've physically removed/opened a wall on the real
# maze since the photo was taken), list it here and it will override the
# detector for that edge only. This does NOT invent a path through a wall
# that's still really there -- it only changes what the solver *thinks*
# is open, so make sure the override matches physical reality before you
# drive the robot.
#
# Edges are given as (row, col, direction) meaning "the wall on the
# `direction` side of cell (row, col)". direction is one of "N","S","E","W".
# Value True = force wall (blocked), False = force open (no wall).
#
# For (1,7) -> (7,1) on this board, the detector found the goal cell sealed
# inside a 16-cell pocket by a *closed loop* of 16 real wall edges (see the
# printed [seal] list below when you run this). Opening ANY ONE of them is
# enough to connect the two regions. Nothing is opened by default --
# uncomment exactly one line below once you've verified (or created) that
# opening on the real board:

